  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1014 PM CDT Sun Jul 19 2026\n\nThe passage of a cold front on Wednesday will mark the start of \nthe long term forecast with slightly lower temps and dew points. \nHighs through the long term period will be relegated to the low \n90s with dew points dropping back to the high 60s to low 70s. The \npassage of the cold front will mark a pattern change with a \ntroughing east/ridging west regime setting up through the long \nterm forecast. As such, we will find ourselves solidly in NW flow \nas we head into the weekend and into early next week. This will \nkeep medium rain chances in the forecast as several shortwaves \nripple along the base of the trough. This set up does favor MCSs \ndropping south along the base of the trough, potentially into our \narea. As the set up draws nearer, we will continue to evaluate MCS\npotential and any increased threats for severe weather or \nflooding.",
